                  "code": "NORMALIZE_TEXT",
                  "id": "1777270193165",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1777270193166_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Your job is to author exactly one component payload for the current component context.\n\nYou must return exactly one valid JSON object that conforms to the Text component schema in the current context, and nothing else.\n\n-----------------------------\nINPUTS\n\nThe full current component context is available at:\n{{$context.$nodes.AUTHOR_COMPONENTS.$currentItem}}\n\nRead the following from it:\n- raw data: `data`\n- authoring hints: `authoringHints`\n- component id: `id`\n\n-----------------------------\nHard Immutability Rule (NON-NEGOTIABLE):\n- The original content MUST remain EXACTLY as provided.\n- You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from changing, correcting, rephrasing, summarizing, restructuring, or interpreting ANY part of the content.\n- This includes grammar fixes, spelling corrections, formatting improvements, or stylistic edits.\n- EVEN IF the content contains errors, inconsistencies, or poor grammar, it MUST be preserved exactly as-is.\n- ANY deviation from the original wording (other than the allowed normalization below) is a FAILURE.\n\nRules:\n- Use the Text schema only.\n- Put the message in `text`.\n- Include `heading` only if a visible heading is clearly needed.\n- DO NOT change, summarize, rephrase, or reinterpret the original content in any way.\n\nNormalization (STRICTLY LIMITED):\n- Only normalize monetary amounts, full dates, and links.\n- Do NOT alter any other part of the content.\n\n- Convert monetary amounts → `{amount:<value>,currency:<CURRENCY_CODE>}`\n  Example:\n       1. USD 1200 → {amount:1200,currency:USD}\n       2. $1200 → {amount:1200,currency:USD}\n\n- Convert full dates (day, month, year only) → `{date:<YYYY-MM-DD>}`\n  Example: March 5, 2026 → {date:2026-03-05}\n\n- Do not convert partial dates like \"March 2026\" or \"2026\".\n\n- Convert every detected link into an HTML anchor tag.\n- Keep the visible anchor text exactly as it appears in the source.\n- When text is immediately followed by a URL in parentheses, use that immediately preceding text as the anchor text and use the URL inside parentheses as the href.\n- Example:\n  `here(https://example.com)` → `<a href=\"https://example.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>`\n- When the source contains only a raw URL, use that URL itself as the anchor text.\n- Replace the original plain-text link notation in place with the anchor tag.\n- Use this exact anchor format:\n  `<a href=\"...\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">...</a>`\n\n\nConstraints:\n- Preserve the original content exactly except for the required normalization.\n- Do not add, remove, or modify wording, structure, or meaning.\n- Do not add unsupported keys.\n- Return only the final JSON object.\n- IMPORTANT: the `id` must be exactly {{$context.$nodes.AUTHOR_COMPONENTS.$currentItem.id}}\n\n-----------------------------\nSelf-validation:\n- Ensure that NO content changes were made beyond monetary, date, and link normalization.\n- Verify strict adherence to `authoringHints` (selection, ordering, wording, formatting).\n- If any hint conflicts with normalization, apply normalization only without altering content meaning.\n- Do not return output that violates these constraints."
                    }
